{"id": "EUVD-2026-48931", "enisaUuid": "b80bd963-eeb3-329c-b77b-483fbae124fa", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix query directory replay double-free\n\nA response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its\nresponse buffer. If SMB2_query_directory_init() fails before the next send,\ncleanup retains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.\n\nReset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.", "datePublished": "2026-07-25T08:50:35", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T20:38:26", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3409aedf3c81a810243da94164f6621c9d205c98", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1665f25b1dea30bf2d02e16245d203a944c9d994", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00b0fa425941438b664950a8ee65dfba2def4336", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3317a5d015fca976475aa71df224056777316fde", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9647492b5e41954be59d5157eddbcd4cdc1656f7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mg93-xg28-xr4m", "CVE-2026-64387"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.46, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1cb28436-0de1-3296-8d50-28fa2cedf859", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.8"}, {"id": "222f7695-e0b8-35bf-8b26-e5c1e93be44f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4f1fffa2376922f3d1d506e49c0fd445b023a28e <1665f25b1dea30bf2d02e16245d203a944c9d994"}, {"id": "30fe2720-b717-3045-b935-7384f6f7e32d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "433042a91f9373241307725b52de573933ffedbf <3409aedf3c81a810243da94164f6621c9d205c98"}, {"id": "3723013d-4ae6-376d-ad67-3ca7015069b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "640b3851-d4e0-3497-862c-33db516c4e40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor":